WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.043
- Welcome back y'all.

00:00:01.043 --> 00:00:03.750
Our next guest spent
decades singing, dancing,

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:05.670
and acting on stage and screen.

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:08.340
Now she is focusing on other
more personal pursuits,

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.020
like being a children's author.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:12.510
Her second book is called
See You On The Other Side,

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:16.170
and it's all about helping kids
cope with change and grief.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:18.540
Everybody, please
welcome back to the show,

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:20.808
Rachel Montez Minor.

00:00:20.808 --> 00:00:25.808
(crowd cheers)
(theme music plays)

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.530
Nice to see you again, how are you?

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:41.430
- I am amazing.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:42.840
New York looks good on you, girl.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.180
- Thank you, I love it here so much.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:46.706
I do.

00:00:46.706 --> 00:00:48.090
It's like given me a whole new life.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:49.073
I love it.

00:00:49.073 --> 00:00:49.906
That's that's what I wanted, so

00:00:49.906 --> 00:00:51.510
thank you God, universe for that.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:52.680
- New York baby!
(crowd cheers)

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:53.610
- How is your hubby?

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:54.930
How's Ricky, how's your daughter?

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:56.490
- [Kelly] Ricky is amazing.

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:58.260
We just came off doing the Kennedy Center.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:00:59.400
- I was like, he's been doing a round,

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:00.510
I've been seeing him everywhere playing-

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:02.640
- You know Ricky, whenever there's music.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.980
And the Emmy's, he was nominated.

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:06.270
And yeah, just getting ready

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:08.160
for like the Clive Davis pre-Grammy.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:09.030
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:10.650
- My daughter's five now

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.930
and it's the most amazing time.

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:14.730
This holiday season was like,

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:16.740
we were in perfect cuteness for Christmas.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.720
It was like the perfect, it was five.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:21.540
She was really believing it was amazing.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:22.710
- Oh, I love that.

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:24.330
And then they open the,
it's just more magical

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:25.520
with kids too, I feel like.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:26.370
It just, I don't know.

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:29.400
It ignites like that kid
in all of us, I feel like.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.233
- Yes.

00:01:30.233 --> 00:01:32.027
She told me "Santa came, but
Rudolph couldn't make it."

00:01:33.681 --> 00:01:34.514
- Dang!

00:01:34.514 --> 00:01:35.557
I was like, "He didn't make it?"

00:01:35.557 --> 00:01:36.906
"No, but Santa came,"

00:01:36.906 --> 00:01:37.770
(both laugh)

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:40.148
- She's like, "I was really bummed."

00:01:40.148 --> 00:01:40.981
I love that.

00:01:40.981 --> 00:01:41.814
Okay, so wait, the book
I think is very important

00:01:41.814 --> 00:01:44.970
because talking about grief,
loss, death, anything like that

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:46.230
with kids, like, I remember my daughter

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:47.637
started, I think around like four.

00:01:47.637 --> 00:01:50.370
Like really talking about
like what, where did they go?

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:51.203
What does this mean?

00:01:51.203 --> 00:01:53.310
And then it starts to freak
them out the older they get.

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:55.050
I think this is such an important book.

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:55.883
- Thank you.

00:01:55.883 --> 00:01:56.850
- So it's called See
You On The Other Side.

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:59.520
So how did this concept hit you?

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.863
- Well, it came to me in a dream.

00:02:03.712 --> 00:02:04.961
- [Kelly] Like the first one!

00:02:04.961 --> 00:02:05.794
- Yes.

00:02:05.794 --> 00:02:06.627
Just like The Sun, The Moon and The Stars.

00:02:06.627 --> 00:02:07.460
That came to me in a dream

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.793
and that was more about our
connection to the universe.

00:02:08.793 --> 00:02:11.670
This one's about our
connection to each other

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:13.320
and how love never ends.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:14.340
- Yeah.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:16.110
I tell my daughter that I,

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.240
it's more my daughter that
gets freaked out about it.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.640
Right now, I don't know if my
son is more aloof about it.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.950
But it really, it terrifies them at first.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.330
And I remember, remember
when you were a kid,

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:25.800
you found out and you
were like, wait, what?

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:27.240
Like what happens?

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:28.080
And it can be terrifying.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.850
So it's so important not
just for kids, this book,

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:31.080
but also for parents to buy,

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.760
to start the conversation with their kids.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:33.593
- Yes.

00:02:33.593 --> 00:02:36.392
And it's really is a
tool to help for any time

00:02:36.392 --> 00:02:37.225
of change, you know?

00:02:37.225 --> 00:02:38.328
It teaches us that change is natural

00:02:38.328 --> 00:02:40.371
and it really connects us to this power

00:02:40.371 --> 00:02:42.810
that love just goes on and on

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:44.760
and it's everlasting.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.372
- Did something happen within your family

00:02:46.372 --> 00:02:48.508
or something, like was
there loss in your family

00:02:48.508 --> 00:02:49.860
to where it kind of triggered that

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:50.910
for you to write something?

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:51.786
- Yes.

00:02:51.786 --> 00:02:53.340
My grandmother and I
were very, very close.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:56.910
She lived to be 96 and she
was a huge part of my...

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:59.275
- Great genetics there, I like that.

00:02:59.275 --> 00:03:00.990
- She's probably 95 there.

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:02.160
Can you believe that skin?

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:03.644
I know.

00:03:03.644 --> 00:03:04.477
But she used to take me to Muir Woods.

00:03:04.477 --> 00:03:06.240
We would travel together
to national parks,

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.257
and my parents both worked full-time jobs,

00:03:08.257 --> 00:03:10.590
so she was a big part of my childhood

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.805
and farmer's markets and dance class.

00:03:12.805 --> 00:03:15.960
So, yeah, I mean, it
came to me in a dream,

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:17.550
but maybe like subconsciously,

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:19.669
because nature is such
a big part of the book

00:03:19.669 --> 00:03:22.470
and teaching them that
change is a part of nature.

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:25.200
So I feel like, you know,
maybe that was her working

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:28.140
through me and in some of the
spreads, you know, in order

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:29.640
to connect with the people we love.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:32.700
Like, I like to cook the
same recipes I made with her,

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:36.720
or we go on the same walks
or go to the same beach.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:38.460
- It's kind of keeping
them alive in a sense.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:39.510
- It is.

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:41.490
And there's lots of like real examples

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:42.716
in the spreads about how to connect

00:03:42.716 --> 00:03:46.350
to those we love and keep
that connection going,

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:49.920
but in a very, like uplifting
and soothing and positive way

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:52.050
and what a gift to give our children.

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:54.450
That, you know, change is, it's natural

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:57.224
and it's positive and
we can stay connected

00:03:57.224 --> 00:03:59.100
to all of those that we love.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:00.180
- Yeah, I agree.

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:01.670
It's a constant conversation
I have with my kids.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:03.530
(audience applauds)

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:04.380
So thank you for the book, everybody,

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:06.630
Rachel's new book is called
See You On The Other Side.

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:09.080
It's out now, get it
wherever you get your books.

